{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011CfgUBfv1HzQ6AfgXnp8qa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 4 pass currently, but the bugs are real — they're just not tested. I can see two issues:\n\n1. **`publish`** stores the date in UTC instead of the author's local timezone. An author in UTC-5 posting at 23:30 local (= 04:30 next UTC day) gets tomorrow's date.\n2. **`display_date`** converts the stored date through the viewer's timezone, which is wrong for a journal — the display date should be the author's intended date, not whatever day that UTC moment falls on in the viewer's zone. The \"anchored at noon UTC\" trick also breaks for UTC+13/+14 viewers.\n\nThe fix: store the author's local date in `publish`, and return it directly in `display_date`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3309,"cache_read_input_tokens":25823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3309},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8825ba5d-6387-48d3-8cb5-0f23ad01d492","uuid":"a4cdb49b-990d-42de-bbd6-cef464e4b4b2","timestamp":"2026-10-04T03:15:12.338Z","request_id":"req_011CfgUBfg8hxPtira2keVS4"}
